Negative control for the transport's own exit (`R7-9`).

Drops the stop control and leaves the rest — step back, play/pause and step
forward all still ask the player for their own call, Live still releases the
track — so the only claim that can go red is the ruled one: a track holding the
surface is stopped from the media bar, not only by picking Live. Picking Live is
a PLAYLIST gesture that happens to release the page; a user looking for a way
out reads it as "choose something else", which is the trap the ruling closed.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: the transport-controls case — the armed bar offers a stop, it emits
`stop`, and it is never disabled.

